      <Desc>Somos La Voz offer free, culturally relevant art and leadership development classes and training to youth in San Diego. We reached approximately 40 young members of our community through programming and approximately 400 community members who attend free pop-up music and art events showcasing the youth art and music.Pan y Paz culinary training program in partnership with a grassroots collective of women entrepreneurs and bakers, baking, food justice, and culinary entrepreneurship classes are offered to community members. We reached approximately 15 women entrepreneurs and 400 community members through community based pop-up events showcasing healthy baked goods.</Desc>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>262852</ExpenseAmt>
        <GrantAmt>48600</GrantAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>5493</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>Via Migrante through partnership with a local coalition of nonprofits, we supported the opening of migrant shelter, and ongoing convening and coalition building between migrant shelters in the region. The program coordinated a meal program at the US/Mexico border providing 12,480 meals and food security support to that shelter for 45 persons.Via Baja: through partnerships with other nonprofits and grassroots groups, we organize groups of microcredit and microfinance lending for women in Baja California. Currently we coordinate 5 solidarity groups, 68 participants. The loan participants repaid loans 100% with interest.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy2Grp>
      <ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
        <ExpenseAmt>190197</ExpenseAmt>
        <RevenueAmt>155954</RevenueAmt>
        <Desc>ViaGO: through partnerships with educational institutions, we receive groups of students and leaders to the region to educate them on community development and the programming of Via throughout the region, through the lens of holistic leadership development. 445 volunteers participated in programs this past year.</Desc>
      </ProgSrvcAccomActy3Grp>
